cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact or paper, please cite it as below."
title: "Where Exactly-Once Ends: Preserving Double-Entry Ledger Invariants When Apache Kafka Pipelines Write to External Stores"
abstract: >-
  An empirical and formal study of the boundary of Kafka's exactly-once semantics when a
  pipeline's side effect lands in an external relational database. The artifact contains a
  fault-injection harness, five mechanism implementations (M0-M4 plus combinations), an
  independent ledger oracle, the full experiment matrix, and the analysis/figure code.
